# yard — pulls in the whole ruby3.3 interpreter (not seeded on this host,
# unlike python3/perl which ship with the base system), so env alone isn't
# enough: /usr/bin/yard's shebang is the absolute host path `#!/usr/bin/ruby`,
# which does not exist outside the prefix ("bad interpreter: No such file or
# directory"). check-package.sh calls it "OK"/direct because its absolute-path
# scan only checks /usr/share|/usr/lib|/usr/libexec|/etc content, not shebang
# lines under /usr/bin — a second check-package.sh gap alongside pmarkdown's
# (interpreter @INC/LOAD_PATH). See #7.
#
# `tools/prefix-run.sh --mode overlay` stacks $PREFIX/usr over the host's
# /usr, so /usr/bin/ruby (and ruby's default vendor_ruby load path) resolve to
# the prefix's copies — no GEM_PATH/GEM_HOME needed once the shebang itself
# resolves.
package  yard
install  ok
tier     overlay
verify   tools/prefix-run.sh yard --version
note     run from the repo root (verify's path is relative to tools/prefix-run.sh)
